> I've recently stopped trying to ascend a monk and decided to work on a 
> rogue. When one dips a dagger in a potion of sickness, poisoning them, is 
> there any real benefit? Do daggers do more damage? Does the sickness wear 
> off after a while? How many times can one dip until a potion is used up?

You get nothing from dipping daggers in a potion of sickness.  The
message is (or should be) Interesting... and the potion is not used
up.  The reason is that daggers are never destroyed from
throwing/firing like darts/arrows/bolts are (permanently poisioned
permanent items would be too powerful).  Dipping a stack of any of
these three will poison the projectiles and use up your potion. 
AFAIK, the poisoning lasts as long as the projectile lasts.  In other
words, the poison never wears off, but the projectiles will break with
[repeated] use.

